# LRCC secrets: a template.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the folder that holds your configuration file: LRCC reads keys from
# there and from nowhere else (ADR-0015), and git ignores .env. Fill in only the keys you have,
# after the "=" with no quotes and no spaces. A variable of the same name set in the environment
# wins over the file. Never put a key anywhere else: not in the configuration file, not in an
# issue, not in a commit. This file itself must keep every value empty.

# Scopus (Elsevier). Key from https://dev.elsevier.com, requested with an institutional e-mail.
# Access also depends on the institution's subscription: requests from its network or VPN, or an
# institutional token that its library requests from Elsevier. From outside, Scopus still answers
# in the STANDARD view, but refuses the COMPLETE view, which carries the abstracts.
SCOPUS_API_KEY=
SCOPUS_INSTTOKEN=

# IEEE Xplore. Key from https://developer.ieee.org: free, approved by hand, with a daily call limit.
# While its status on that site is "waiting", every request is refused with "Developer Inactive".
IEEE_API_KEY=

# PubMed (NCBI). Optional: raises the limit from three to ten requests per second.
# From the NCBI account settings, under API Key Management.
NCBI_API_KEY=
